IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-danger-railways-vehicles`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-danger-railways-vehicles.l4
-- (sections 32 to 35).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before
-- the assertion was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: sections 32 to 35`

§§ `Section 32`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, put/threw on a railway, took up a rail, turned points,
-- made/showed/hid/removed a signal or light, did any other matter or thing, intended to
-- endanger the safety of a person travelling or upon the railway
`s32 put a stone on the line` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 took up a rail` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 turned the points` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 showed a false signal` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 any other matter or thing` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s32 put a stone on the line, no intent to endanger` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s32 intent to endanger, no act` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s32 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 32` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 put a stone on the line`
#ASSERT `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 took up a rail`
#ASSERT `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 turned the points`
#ASSERT `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 showed a false signal`
#ASSERT `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 any other matter or thing`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 put a stone on the line, no intent to endanger`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 intent to endanger, no act`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` `s32 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 32: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 32: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 33`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, threw (or caused to fall or strike) a thing at a railway
-- engine/carriage/truck, intended to injure a person in it, intended to endanger a person in it
`s33 threw, intent to injure` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s33 threw, intent to endanger` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s33 threw, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s33 intent, did not throw` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s33 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s33 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 33` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 threw, intent to injure`
#ASSERT `s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 threw, intent to endanger`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 threw, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 intent, did not throw`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` `s33 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 33: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 33: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 34`

-- did an unlawful act, wilfully omitted or neglected, endangered the safety of a person
-- on a railway, aided or assisted in that
`s34 unlawful act, endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s34 wilful omission, endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s34 unlawful act, aided or assisted` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s34 wilful omission, aided or assisted` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s34 unlawful act, nobody endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s34 endangered, neither act nor wilful omission` MEANS `Conduct under section 34` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 unlawful act, endangered`
#ASSERT `s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 wilful omission, endangered`
#ASSERT `s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 unlawful act, aided or assisted`
#ASSERT `s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 wilful omission, aided or assisted`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 unlawful act, nobody endangered`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34: endangering railway passengers` `s34 endangered, neither act nor wilful omission`)
#ASSERT `s 34: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
-- two years = 24 months
#ASSERT `s 34: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 35`

-- had the charge of a carriage or vehicle, wanton or furious driving or racing, other
-- wilful misconduct, wilful neglect, did or caused bodily harm
`s35 furious driving` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s35 wilful misconduct` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s35 wilful neglect` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s35 furious driving, nobody hurt` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s35 not in charge` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s35 harm, none of the three` MEANS `Conduct under section 35` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 furious driving`
#ASSERT `s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 wilful misconduct`
#ASSERT `s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 wilful neglect`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 furious driving, nobody hurt`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 not in charge`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` `s35 harm, none of the three`)
#ASSERT `s 35: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 35: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)
